## Working with the Rust bindings

This project includes a native extension written in Rust. The performance-critical work lives in a Cargo workspace under `crates/`:

- `crates/{{ python_package_name }}_core` — a plain Rust library with the core routines (unit-tested with `cargo test`)
- `crates/{{ python_package_name }}_python` — a thin [PyO3](https://pyo3.rs/) layer that exposes them to Python as the native module `{{ python_package_name }}._native`

The Python package under `src/{{ python_package_name }}/` calls into the compiled extension, so build it into your environment before running the Python code:

```sh
# build the native extension into the active uv environment
uv run maturin develop

# or use the provided poe task
uv run poe develop
```

`uv run poe test` rebuilds the extension and runs the Python tests; `uv run poe pipeline` runs the Rust tests, rebuilds, lints, and runs the Python tests. See the [versioning notes]({{ github_url }}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#versioning) for how release versions flow from git tags into the built wheel.

